   EBaC (Electronic Bible and Concordance)
   written by Neil G. Brookins
   http://ebac.sourceforge.net/

To build from source,
1) Read the comments in the makefile. Edit as needed.
2) type: make
3) set the environment variable BIBLEROOT to the location of the EBaC files.
	for bash shell: export BIBLEROOT=/home/dirname/ebac-1.3.0
	this directory must contain the text file 'trans' as in translations.
	the first column in 'trans' must be a valid subdirectory.
	For example, AV is a subdirectory of $BIBLEROOT
	Folder 'AV' must contain a text file 'booklist'
	The names in 'booklist' must be valid text file names.
4) Run the program: ./bible

To add new translations, such as NIV, NLT, NKJV, etc,
1) Place the Bible text files in a subdirectory of BIBLEROOT.
2) Add a new line to 'trans' for each translation with the matching name.
	NIV  New International Version
	NLT  New Living Translation
	NKJV New King James Version
3) Change to the new directory and generate a new index for each one.
	cd $BIBLEROOT/NIV;  ../index
	cd $BIBLEROOT/NLT;  ../index
	cd $BIBLEROOT/NKJV; ../index
	The index generator read/writes to the current directory only.
4) Run the program: cd $BIBLEROOT; ./bible
	You will now see all the translation choices in the "Change translation" menu.

